p.membercontribution:
 said that the Supplementary Estimate was double the original, so that evidently the latter was absolutely misleading. Who made out the Estimates? Was it the Minister in charge of the Department, or was it some official? They noticed that as one Minister went out a new Minister came in, and, if all reports were true, there was seemingly no difficulty at all about that in view of the number of applications to fill the position. What he would like to know was, how and where this money was spent? Were the troops employed in China all British;

1073
were they white troops, for after all the declared and avowed policy of the Government was Imperialistic? They declared chat they were the pillars of the Empire; that they held up the Empire; and that they hoped to bring the Colonies together. In bringing troops to China, did they bring all British troops?

section.p:
Blyth and Cowpen Gas Bill; Whitby Gas Bill. Reported, with Amendments;

1153
Reports to lie upon the Table, and to be printed.
